msgid "【注意】A2系列产品UB大小为192KB(1572864bit)。"
msgstr "[Note] The UB size of A2 series products is 192KB(1572864bit)."

msgid "通用单核数据运算"
msgstr "General single-core data computation"

msgid "开发目标"
msgstr "Development Objectives"

msgid ""
"在昇腾NPU单核上实现基础数据运算算子（如加减乘除、激活函数、简单矩阵元素运算）。保证算子在单核内高效执行，为后续多核并行和分布式扩展打下基础。"
msgstr ""
"Implement basic data operation operators (such as addition, subtraction, "
"multiplication, division, activation functions, and simple matrix element-"
"wise operations) on a single Ascend NPU core. Ensure the operators execute "
"efficiently within a single core, laying the foundation for subsequent "
"multi-core parallelism and distributed scaling."

msgid "开发步骤"
msgstr "Development Steps"

msgid "确定算子功能  -明确输入/输出张量的形状、数据类型（float16/float32/int32等）。  -确认是否需要广播、边界处理。"
msgstr ""
"Determine the operator functionality  -Specify the shape and data type (such"
" as float16, float32, and int32) of the input/output tensors.  -Confirm "
"whether broadcasting and boundary handling are required."

msgid "编写核函数（kernel）  单核运算通常对应块级的数据处理。  单核数据运算示例：向量加法"
msgstr ""
"Writing a kernel  Single-core computation usually corresponds to block-level"
" data processing.  Single-core data computation example: vector addition"

msgid ""
"\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def add_kernel(x_ptr, # Pointer to first input vector.\n"
"    y_ptr, # Pointer to second input vector.\n"
"    output_ptr, # output 向量的指针.\n"
"    n_elements, # 向量的大小.\n"
"    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr, # 每个进程需要处理的元素个数.\n"
"    # 注意：constexpr属性表示它可以被用作shape值.\n"
"):\n"
"    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0) # We use a 1D launch grid so axis is 0.\n"
"    block_start = pid * BLOCK_SIZE\n"
"    offsets = block_start + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n"
"    mask = offsets < n_elements\n"
"    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask)\n"
"    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask)\n"
"    output = x + y\n"
"    tl.store(output_ptr + offsets, output, mask=mask)"
msgstr ""
"@triton.jit\n"
"def add_kernel(x_ptr, # Pointer to first input vector.\n"
"    y_ptr, # Pointer to second input vector.\n"
"    output_ptr, # Pointer to the output vector.\n"
"    n_elements, # Size of the vector.\n"
"    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr, # Number of elements each program needs to process.\n"
"    # Note: The constexpr attribute indicates that it can be used as a shape value.\n"
"):\n"
"    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0) # We use a 1D launch grid so axis is 0.\n"
"    block_start = pid * BLOCK_SIZE\n"
"    offsets = block_start + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n"
"    mask = offsets < n_elements\n"
"    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask)\n"
"    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask)\n"
"    output = x + y\n"
"    tl.store(output_ptr + offsets, output, mask=mask)"

msgid "调用："
msgstr "Call:"

msgid ""
"def add(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor):\n"
"    output = torch.empty_like(x)\n"
"    n_elements = output.numel()\n"
"    grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n_elements, meta['BLOCK_SIZE']), )\n"
"    add_kernel[grid](x, y, output, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE=1024)\n"
"    return output\n"
msgstr ""
"def add(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor):\n"
"    output = torch.empty_like(x)\n"
"    n_elements = output.numel()\n"
"    grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n_elements, meta['BLOCK_SIZE']), )\n"
"    add_kernel[grid](x, y, output, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE=1024)\n"
"    return output\n"

msgid "使用上述函数计算两个 torch.tensor 对象的 element-wise sum，并测试其正确性"
msgstr ""
"Use the above function to compute the element-wise sum of two torch.tensor "
